WEBVTT

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.604
♪ ♪

00:00:24.158 --> 00:00:25.393
&lt;i&gt;MARINER:
Hey, hey, hey!&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:25.493 --> 00:00:27.027
Come on, you're sparking
the raktajino.

00:00:27.128 --> 00:00:27.960
Sorry.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.263
Maybe take a break?

00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:31.699
Since we're,
you know, on a break.

00:00:31.799 --> 00:00:33.166
I've been trying
to connect my oculus

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:34.802
to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; systems
all morning.

00:00:34.902 --> 00:00:36.537
They used to work just fine,
but something's off--

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:37.805
(shouts)

00:00:37.905 --> 00:00:39.140
- Boimler!
- I'm okay!

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.574
I'm okay.
(chuckles)

00:00:40.674 --> 00:00:42.510
Ah, since when can that thing
shoot plasma?

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.212
It's not supposed to.

00:00:44.312 --> 00:00:45.879
(groans)
Particle headache.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:48.048
Hey, careful, Ruthy,
this is our last Boimler.

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:49.350
We don't got any more
after this.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.651
Hmm, you have experienced
duplication?

00:00:51.652 --> 00:00:53.653
Oh, yeah, he got
transporter cloned.

00:00:53.654 --> 00:00:55.223
The other one
called himself William

00:00:55.323 --> 00:00:56.924
to kiss Riker's butt,
but then he got killed

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.058
by some random gas.

00:00:58.192 --> 00:00:59.293
(clears throat)

00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:00.628
Uh, but, you know,

00:01:00.728 --> 00:01:02.329
people are always
coming back to life.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.432
Shaxs exploded
and he's doing great.

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:07.135
(shouting gibberish)

00:01:07.235 --> 00:01:08.236
It's okay.

00:01:08.336 --> 00:01:09.836
Sometimes
the randomness of death

00:01:09.837 --> 00:01:11.772
matches the unexpected joys
of life.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.907
I still can't believe
he stayed on the &lt;i&gt;Titan.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.409
That was one motivated Boimler.

00:01:15.509 --> 00:01:16.377
Yeah.

00:01:16.477 --> 00:01:17.745
I mean, if he were still around,

00:01:17.845 --> 00:01:19.679
I'd bet he'd be
in some huge adventure.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.515
I wish I could've seen it.

00:01:22.516 --> 00:01:24.785
♪ ♪

00:01:35.062 --> 00:01:36.229
90 seconds to the rift.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.132
Weapons armed and ready.

00:01:38.232 --> 00:01:40.367
Prepare to cross
the quantum threshold.

00:01:40.368 --> 00:01:41.401
Again.

00:01:41.402 --> 00:01:42.603
Let's do this!

00:01:42.736 --> 00:01:44.472
♪

00:01:50.278 --> 00:01:53.247
&lt;i&gt;WILLIAM:
Captain's log, William Boimler
of the&lt;/i&gt; Anaximander.

00:01:53.347 --> 00:01:55.916
&lt;i&gt;Stardate, uh, confidential.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:56.016 --> 00:01:58.018
&lt;i&gt;I've been ordered
to find and stop&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.488
&lt;i&gt;whomever's been trying
to destroy the multiverse.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:00.588 --> 00:02:02.889
&lt;i&gt;But I find my enthusiasm...&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.325
&lt;i&gt;waning.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:06.393
&lt;i&gt;While I'm not authorized
to name the organization&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:06.394 --> 00:02:09.096
&lt;i&gt;that faked my death
and sent me diving into rifts,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:09.197 --> 00:02:13.167
&lt;i&gt;I can talk about my crew
of interdimensional castaways.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:15.336
&lt;i&gt;T'Pol, my Vulcan first officer,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:15.469 --> 00:02:16.970
&lt;i&gt;is an expert on human emotions&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:17.104 --> 00:02:19.105
&lt;i&gt;after being married
to Trip Tucker for decades.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:19.106 --> 00:02:21.809
&lt;i&gt;My tactical officer
is Curzon Dax&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:21.942 --> 00:02:23.644
&lt;i&gt;from a reality
where he hasn't yet passed&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:23.777 --> 00:02:25.813
&lt;i&gt;- his symbiont to Jadzia.&lt;/i&gt;
- (Dax shouting)

00:02:25.946 --> 00:02:29.183
&lt;i&gt;Prone to injury, he's lucky
we have Elim Garak,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:29.317 --> 00:02:31.118
&lt;i&gt;a brilliant Cardassian surgeon.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:31.219 --> 00:02:34.188
&lt;i&gt;And his husband,
an emergency medical hologram&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:34.322 --> 00:02:35.989
&lt;i&gt;based on Dr. Julian Bashir.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:36.123 --> 00:02:38.692
&lt;i&gt;Everyone on this crew are from
totally different realities,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:38.792 --> 00:02:40.694
&lt;i&gt;but we make a great team.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:40.828 --> 00:02:42.762
Okay, give me good news, Dax.

00:02:42.763 --> 00:02:43.796
Negative.

00:02:43.797 --> 00:02:45.366
No sign of the mole rat.

00:02:45.466 --> 00:02:47.435
There is a Starfleet escape pod.

00:02:47.535 --> 00:02:48.936
I am reading a single lifeform.

00:02:49.036 --> 00:02:51.239
Who will it be,
Neelix with a crew cut?

00:02:51.339 --> 00:02:53.341
&lt;i&gt;Really big Spock?&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:58.212 --> 00:02:59.713
Ooh, thanks for the save.

00:02:59.847 --> 00:03:01.614
- I thought I was a goner.
- WILLIAM: What a surprise.

00:03:01.615 --> 00:03:03.484
Another Harry Kim.

00:03:03.584 --> 00:03:05.219
What do you mean another?

00:03:05.319 --> 00:03:07.355
Most of the crew are Harry Kims.

00:03:07.455 --> 00:03:09.623
- Ah, who's this handsome guy?
- Hey, Harry!

00:03:09.723 --> 00:03:10.891
The Kim crew is thriving.

00:03:10.991 --> 00:03:12.226
- High five, baby!
- (whooping)

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.262
I'm so sick
of the (bleep) multiverse.

00:03:14.362 --> 00:03:17.598
HARRY KIMS (chanting):
Kim! Kim! Kim! Kim! Kim!

00:03:18.399 --> 00:03:20.568
♪ ♪

00:03:37.818 --> 00:03:39.953
♪ ♪

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:16.357
♪ ♪

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.869
♪ ♪

00:04:34.442 --> 00:04:35.876
- Have at thee!
- Repairs to the rift

00:04:35.976 --> 00:04:37.478
are underway, Captain.

00:04:37.578 --> 00:04:38.946
(grunting)

00:04:39.046 --> 00:04:40.681
Must you do that on the bridge?

00:04:40.781 --> 00:04:42.149
You'll thank me when someone

00:04:42.249 --> 00:04:44.318
needs to be chopped.
(grunts)

00:04:44.418 --> 00:04:46.820
I thought the dimensional rifts
were natural occurrences.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.254
Who exactly are you chasing?

00:04:48.255 --> 00:04:49.623
We don't know.

00:04:49.723 --> 00:04:51.758
But someone has it out
for the multiverse.

00:04:51.759 --> 00:04:54.962
They have a ship that bridges
dimensions by tearing them open.

00:04:55.062 --> 00:04:57.631
Whoa, whoa, whoa! There's
more than two dimensions?

00:04:57.765 --> 00:04:59.933
Starfleet believes
that there are

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:02.336
an infinite amount
of quantum realities.

00:05:02.436 --> 00:05:04.171
Each is represented by a sphere.

00:05:04.271 --> 00:05:06.173
DAX:
It's like a bubble bath.

00:05:06.273 --> 00:05:07.975
But the bubbles are universes.

00:05:08.075 --> 00:05:10.578
The ship we're chasing
is ripping open the bubbles.

00:05:10.678 --> 00:05:12.480
Creating rifts
which weaken the integrity

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:13.981
of all quantum realities.

00:05:14.081 --> 00:05:16.149
Why would someone want
to destroy reality?

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:18.785
Because they're probably
a hacky evil version

00:05:18.786 --> 00:05:20.287
of someone we all know.

00:05:20.388 --> 00:05:23.657
A reverse Picard or
Borgified Kirk or (bleep) it,

00:05:23.757 --> 00:05:25.359
I don't know, human Worf.

00:05:25.459 --> 00:05:26.794
That's all the multiverse is!

00:05:26.894 --> 00:05:29.497
Just lazy derivative remixes!

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:30.998
(William growls)

00:05:31.098 --> 00:05:32.700
Did I say something wrong?

00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:35.235
The captain's patience
has been waning.

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:37.937
Yeah, all the dimension hopping
and no bad guy

00:05:37.938 --> 00:05:39.607
has to feel like treading water.

00:05:39.707 --> 00:05:42.175
That is an astute simile,
Mr. Kim.

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:43.844
Thanks.

00:05:46.514 --> 00:05:48.315
GARAK: In some dimensions,
I'm a tailor...

00:05:48.416 --> 00:05:50.350
Are they from the same reality?

00:05:50.451 --> 00:05:52.486
No, but they love
to brag about how

00:05:52.586 --> 00:05:54.722
statistically unlikely
their marriage is.

00:05:54.822 --> 00:05:57.925
Lovers never fall
out of the rifts for Curzon!

00:05:58.025 --> 00:06:01.662
It must be cool seeing all kinds
of wacky new dimensions.

00:06:01.762 --> 00:06:04.131
I wonder why the captain
hates it so much.

00:06:04.231 --> 00:06:06.132
He's used
to exploring the galaxy.

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:08.536
Now he just goes
from rift to rift.

00:06:08.636 --> 00:06:10.336
KIM 1:
Harry!

00:06:10.337 --> 00:06:12.372
Always great to have
another Kim aboard.

00:06:12.473 --> 00:06:13.907
Did your &lt;i&gt;Voyager&lt;/i&gt;
get back to Earth

00:06:14.007 --> 00:06:16.410
or did you, like, settle
in the Delta Quadrant?

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:17.545
We got back.

00:06:17.645 --> 00:06:19.346
- Dude!
- Told ya.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:19.447 --> 00:06:21.682
(gasps) Wait, everyone shut up!

00:06:21.782 --> 00:06:24.384
This Kim's got two pips!

00:06:24.485 --> 00:06:25.686
- Whoa.
- No way!

00:06:25.786 --> 00:06:27.354
You're a full lieutenant?

00:06:27.455 --> 00:06:29.022
Yeah. Wait.

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:31.258
You're all still ensigns?

00:06:31.358 --> 00:06:33.226
That's (bleep) up.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.396
I was reading
about the original Dr. Bashir.

00:06:36.497 --> 00:06:38.899
Apparently he was
an avid racquetball player.

00:06:38.999 --> 00:06:41.735
He and Chief O'Brien were
quite competitive.

00:06:41.835 --> 00:06:43.103
Did they ever invite you
to join?

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:45.573
I took an oath to do no harm.

00:06:45.673 --> 00:06:48.841
Which includes humiliating
my patients at racquetball.

00:06:48.842 --> 00:06:50.410
- (grunts)
- (Bashir gasps)

00:06:50.511 --> 00:06:52.880
Is it your shoulder again?

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:54.815
Oh, there was a Bolian masseuse

00:06:54.915 --> 00:06:56.950
on the promenade
who had magical hands.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.586
I'll take you when this is over.

00:06:58.686 --> 00:07:01.421
Photonic beings don't really
benefit from massage.

00:07:01.522 --> 00:07:04.692
Wait, what makes you think we'll
be living in your reality?!

00:07:04.792 --> 00:07:06.760
Darling, I haven't thought
about it at all.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.362
Oh, yes, you have. I know
how you operate, Elim Garak.

00:07:09.463 --> 00:07:11.899
Our future home reality
is still up in the air.

00:07:11.999 --> 00:07:13.601
My shoulder still has a knot.

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:16.670
Well, then it's a pity
your Bolian isn't here to help.

00:07:17.871 --> 00:07:20.007
♪ ♪

00:07:22.109 --> 00:07:23.977
The rift is almost repaired.

00:07:24.077 --> 00:07:25.745
Yeah, keep it up.
I'm sure our friend

00:07:25.746 --> 00:07:27.581
will be opening
a new one soon enough.

00:07:27.681 --> 00:07:28.882
(alert sounding)

00:07:28.982 --> 00:07:31.284
Something just rocketed
through the rift.

00:07:31.418 --> 00:07:32.585
T'POL:
A Starfleet shuttle craft.

00:07:32.586 --> 00:07:33.787
Its engines are critical.

00:07:33.887 --> 00:07:35.155
They must've been
traveling at warp.

00:07:35.255 --> 00:07:37.190
Emergency transport now!

00:07:42.429 --> 00:07:43.797
(gasps)
Mariner!

00:07:43.931 --> 00:07:44.998
Whoa!

00:07:45.132 --> 00:07:46.066
What in the--? What--?

00:07:46.166 --> 00:07:47.200
Where am--? How did y--?

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:48.736
(gasps)
Boims?

00:07:48.836 --> 00:07:51.004
I think that's T'Pol.

00:07:58.278 --> 00:08:00.080
Wait. Wait, wait, wait, so...

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:02.248
you're a clone of a Boimler
from another reality,

00:08:02.249 --> 00:08:04.250
so you've got, like,
a backup Boimler at home?

00:08:04.251 --> 00:08:05.586
He's not a backup.

00:08:05.686 --> 00:08:06.987
We were transporter duplicated.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.955
No way, that happened
to my Troi.

00:08:08.956 --> 00:08:11.324
Yeah, her copy was stranded
on a planet for years.

00:08:11.424 --> 00:08:12.459
(laughs)
That sounds familiar.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:13.727
That happened to my Riker, too.

00:08:13.827 --> 00:08:15.062
Do you have a Tendi
and a Rutherford?

00:08:15.162 --> 00:08:18.498
Yeah, but I haven't seen them
in ages.

00:08:18.599 --> 00:08:20.200
What's your Boimler like?

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:22.635
Oh, he's the best. Still
an ensign, gets in his own way.

00:08:22.636 --> 00:08:24.437
He wears a leather jacket
at all times,

00:08:24.538 --> 00:08:26.006
which is weird,
but we're used to it.

00:08:26.106 --> 00:08:28.307
Like, like, he sleeps in it.
What's your Mariner like?

00:08:28.308 --> 00:08:30.377
Uh, you know, she's a fearless
adventurer like you.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.946
(chuckles) Yeah, right,
I am not really a fan of danger

00:08:33.046 --> 00:08:35.515
or away missions or anything
that involves phasers.

00:08:35.616 --> 00:08:38.451
I'd rather be tinkering
with plasma coils.

00:08:38.552 --> 00:08:40.453
What's with the look?

00:08:40.554 --> 00:08:41.722
Huh? N-Nothing.

00:08:41.855 --> 00:08:43.857
It's just really nice
having you here.

00:08:43.991 --> 00:08:45.458
Yeah, I'm pretty great.

00:08:45.559 --> 00:08:47.060
What's it like having
your own quarters?

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.696
Does Janeway ever
let you sit in the big chair?

00:08:48.796 --> 00:08:51.330
Of course! How have
none of you ever been promoted?

00:08:51.331 --> 00:08:53.667
You know, I guess between
all the Borg infiltrations

00:08:53.767 --> 00:08:55.402
and aliens trying
to steal our organs,

00:08:55.502 --> 00:08:56.870
it didn't seem
like that big of a deal.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.805
We're just happy
to be in Starfleet.

00:08:58.806 --> 00:09:00.273
I ran into the same thing.

00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:02.442
Everybody gets promoted
before ops.

00:09:02.542 --> 00:09:04.544
It's like nobody knows
what we do.

00:09:04.678 --> 00:09:06.379
Ooh, what did you guys do
with your Tuvoks?

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:09.116
Oh, great, my favorite Vulcan.

00:09:09.216 --> 00:09:11.752
I was married to a human
for 63 years.

00:09:11.852 --> 00:09:13.653
I know sarcasm when I hear it.

00:09:13.654 --> 00:09:15.188
I don't need a know-it-all

00:09:15.288 --> 00:09:17.758
picking me apart while
I'm trying to eat. (slurps)

00:09:17.858 --> 00:09:20.227
Are you sure you should be
consuming that much sodium?

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.329
What do you even know
about the Trill diet?

00:09:22.429 --> 00:09:24.064
I know that you carry
the Dax symbiont,

00:09:24.197 --> 00:09:26.399
which must be protected
for its next host,

00:09:26.533 --> 00:09:28.568
of which there is none
on the &lt;i&gt;Anaximander.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:28.669 --> 00:09:32.840
Oh, thank you so much
for explaining that to me,

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.407
you smug Vulcan &lt;i&gt;petaQ.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:34.541 --> 00:09:36.610
Your anger masks a fear
that I am correct.

00:09:36.744 --> 00:09:39.246
Perhaps you should moderate
your eating habits.

00:09:39.346 --> 00:09:41.248
Look, I live life to its fullest

00:09:41.348 --> 00:09:44.016
so the next Dax can actually
learn something.

00:09:44.017 --> 00:09:45.619
Sodium is not a full life.

00:09:45.719 --> 00:09:46.887
Maybe it is for me, damn it!

00:09:46.987 --> 00:09:48.622
Wait, wait, wait,
if you hate danger,

00:09:48.722 --> 00:09:50.858
then why did I have to rescue
you from your own shuttle?

00:09:50.958 --> 00:09:53.260
(slurps) I didn't know the rifts
emitted radial tachyons.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.796
Yeah. No warping or they make
your engines explode.

00:09:55.929 --> 00:09:57.430
Ugh, yeah, that was bad.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.199
But the good news is,
now I know how to track the guy

00:09:59.299 --> 00:10:00.400
who's screwing up
the multiverse.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.270
- What?
- (yelps) Don't do that.

00:10:04.404 --> 00:10:05.939
&lt;i&gt;MARINER:
Back on my&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos,
&lt;i&gt;I was trying&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:06.039 --> 00:10:08.308
to figure out why
our entanglement processor

00:10:08.408 --> 00:10:09.777
kept needing a reset.

00:10:09.877 --> 00:10:11.543
Turns out, something was
(bleep) up the superposition.

00:10:11.544 --> 00:10:14.614
- The transdimensional rifts.
- Yup. Every time

00:10:14.715 --> 00:10:16.316
one gets opened,
a second one appears

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:18.652
in some random other part
of the galaxy.

00:10:18.786 --> 00:10:19.953
Conservation of energy.

00:10:20.087 --> 00:10:21.621
Each universe
has a finite amount.

00:10:21.755 --> 00:10:23.556
If you create a rift...

00:10:23.657 --> 00:10:26.459
T'POL:
Another must open to accommodate
the energy being pushed out.

00:10:26.559 --> 00:10:28.528
MARINER:
So they're opening a rift,
closing it up,

00:10:28.628 --> 00:10:31.498
and we're going to the wrong one
way the hell far away.

00:10:31.631 --> 00:10:33.000
That's why we've
never caught up.

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:34.802
We've been going
to the wrong rifts.

00:10:34.902 --> 00:10:37.805
Every rift they open creates a
huge influx of radial tachyons,

00:10:37.905 --> 00:10:40.140
but if we recreated
those levels first...

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:43.243
WILLIAM:
It would force their next rift
to open right here.

00:10:43.343 --> 00:10:44.678
Where we'll be waiting.

00:10:44.812 --> 00:10:46.578
Mariner,
you're a great engineer.

00:10:46.579 --> 00:10:48.247
Mm, why do you sound
so surprised?

00:10:48.248 --> 00:10:49.783
Sorry.

00:10:55.188 --> 00:10:56.990
Radial tachyon levels
are still rising.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.993
Trap is set.
Let's see if this works.

00:11:00.093 --> 00:11:03.430
Come on, you little sneak.
Show yourself.

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:05.264
Are the shields raised?
Because this is feeling

00:11:05.265 --> 00:11:07.835
like a "calm before the storm"
type sitch.

00:11:10.738 --> 00:11:12.505
Holy crap, it worked.

00:11:12.605 --> 00:11:13.774
(alert sounding)

00:11:13.874 --> 00:11:15.408
T'POL:
Captain, Mariner's plan

00:11:15.508 --> 00:11:16.777
appears to have been successful.

00:11:16.877 --> 00:11:17.778
WILLIAM:
They're running.

00:11:17.878 --> 00:11:19.346
Dax, target their engines.

00:11:22.716 --> 00:11:24.150
&lt;i&gt;DAX:
Direct hit. (gasps)&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:24.151 --> 00:11:25.886
They don't have shields?

00:11:30.623 --> 00:11:33.393
They are attempting to escape
by creating a new rift.

00:11:33.526 --> 00:11:35.262
Set a pursuit course.
Full impulse.

00:11:35.362 --> 00:11:36.897
The event horizon is in flux.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:39.232
Our structural integrity
will be damaged.

00:11:39.366 --> 00:11:40.667
We don't have a choice.

00:11:42.335 --> 00:11:43.937
I hate this part.

00:11:44.037 --> 00:11:45.806
I love it.

00:11:48.375 --> 00:11:49.576
(laughs)

00:11:50.677 --> 00:11:52.645
(groans, shouts)

00:12:00.187 --> 00:12:02.521
- Medic, we got
a battle-damaged Kim here.
- (groaning)

00:12:02.522 --> 00:12:05.759
These Harry Kims are stronger
than they look. He'll be fine.

00:12:05.893 --> 00:12:08.728
In my reality,
Risa has an entire moon

00:12:08.829 --> 00:12:11.064
devoted to growing
heirloom grapes.

00:12:11.164 --> 00:12:12.732
The wine is exquisite.

00:12:12.833 --> 00:12:15.969
My Risa has two vineyard moons.
Uh, close that artery, will you?

00:12:16.069 --> 00:12:18.305
Each moon has
multiple varietals.

00:12:18.405 --> 00:12:19.839
I... I don't care.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.909
You will once you taste
their reds.

00:12:22.009 --> 00:12:23.443
You can't just
unilaterally decide

00:12:23.576 --> 00:12:25.846
that we're moving to
your reality. It's not fair.

00:12:25.946 --> 00:12:27.880
I let you choose what I had
for dinner last night.

00:12:27.881 --> 00:12:31.584
Well, that doesn't equal a
lifetime in a strange universe.

00:12:31.718 --> 00:12:32.986
My universe isn't strange,

00:12:33.086 --> 00:12:35.022
and you aren't even
made of carbon, my love.

00:12:35.122 --> 00:12:36.022
Why do you care?

00:12:36.023 --> 00:12:38.458
Oh, pulling the hologram card.

00:12:38.558 --> 00:12:40.427
Forgive me. I take it back.

00:12:40.527 --> 00:12:42.561
My emotions
got the better of me.

00:12:42.562 --> 00:12:46.032
Hopefully, your emotions enjoy
sleeping on the ground tonight.

00:12:46.033 --> 00:12:48.568
This hologram will be
in bed, alone.

00:12:49.302 --> 00:12:51.138
- Ugh, humans.
- Huh?

00:12:51.271 --> 00:12:52.806
Oh, not you.

00:12:56.143 --> 00:12:57.477
&lt;i&gt;DAX:
We're in weapons range.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:57.577 --> 00:12:59.079
Permission to blast
these &lt;i&gt;biHnuchs.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:59.179 --> 00:13:00.613
I don't think that's
such a good idea in the rift.

00:13:00.713 --> 00:13:02.816
- This is our only chance.
- Dax, wait!

00:13:07.454 --> 00:13:08.989
(crackling)

00:13:12.759 --> 00:13:15.795
Please tell me
they didn't get away.

00:13:15.896 --> 00:13:17.229
Thanks to Curzon's
insubordination,

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.932
they were forced to make
an emergency landing.

00:13:19.032 --> 00:13:20.500
DAX:
Good.

00:13:22.335 --> 00:13:23.470
WILLIAM:
Take us down.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.005
We have repairs of our own
to make.

00:13:25.138 --> 00:13:27.073
Don't glare at me. We got them.

00:13:27.074 --> 00:13:28.575
We (bleep) better.

00:13:28.675 --> 00:13:30.878
Ugh. Man, my Boimler's
way chiller than this one.

00:13:30.978 --> 00:13:33.745
I do not have a Boimler
in my quantum reality

00:13:33.746 --> 00:13:35.281
in order to make a comparison.

00:13:35.282 --> 00:13:37.217
Oh, he's a big Starfleet nerd
like Archer.

00:13:37.317 --> 00:13:38.318
You had one of those, right?

00:13:38.418 --> 00:13:39.752
Yes.

00:13:39.853 --> 00:13:43.356
And "big Starfleet nerd"
is an accurate description.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:53.033
Ugh, stupid bog planets
are the worst.

00:13:53.166 --> 00:13:55.468
They're just wet
and cold and sad.

00:13:55.568 --> 00:13:57.004
Ugh. How far do we have to wade?

00:13:57.104 --> 00:13:59.372
Their landing site is roughly
400 meters to the north.

00:13:59.506 --> 00:14:00.772
Keep your heads up.

00:14:00.773 --> 00:14:01.909
We don't know anything
about this reality.

00:14:02.009 --> 00:14:03.176
(gasps)

00:14:04.878 --> 00:14:06.312
- (chirps)
- MARINER: Oh, no way.

00:14:06.313 --> 00:14:07.714
I know these guys.
They're super nice.

00:14:07.814 --> 00:14:08.681
We must be on Khwopa.

00:14:08.781 --> 00:14:09.849
Hey, what's up, my man?

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.919
- (roars)
- (Mariner gasps, screams)

00:14:12.552 --> 00:14:13.887
(groans)

00:14:13.987 --> 00:14:15.255
(gasps)

00:14:15.355 --> 00:14:17.289
(grunts)

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:18.825
(gasps)

00:14:18.926 --> 00:14:20.994
I'm starting to see
why you hate the multiverse.

00:14:21.094 --> 00:14:22.362
Hey, you guys aren't mad

00:14:22.462 --> 00:14:24.163
about the stuff I said
about bogs, right?

00:14:24.164 --> 00:14:26.199
'Cause I love bogs.
Uh, live long and...

00:14:26.299 --> 00:14:27.534
(both gasp)

00:14:34.341 --> 00:14:36.676
- (screams, sighs)
- (hisses)

00:14:36.809 --> 00:14:37.777
You Kims okay?

00:14:37.877 --> 00:14:40.280
Yeah, just a little soggy.

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:42.682
Feral Khwopians
don't make any sense.

00:14:42.782 --> 00:14:44.151
They're too cute to be mean.

00:14:44.251 --> 00:14:46.686
At least they aren't trying
to drink our bones.

00:14:46.786 --> 00:14:47.988
(Mariner whimpers)

00:14:48.088 --> 00:14:49.389
- (hyperventilating)
- WILLIAM: You okay?

00:14:49.522 --> 00:14:50.557
I've never been
in a prison before.

00:14:50.657 --> 00:14:51.858
It's kind of freaking me out.

00:14:51.959 --> 00:14:53.326
(screams)

00:14:54.227 --> 00:14:55.695
WILLIAM:
(gasps) A human?

00:14:55.795 --> 00:14:56.863
What're you doing here?

00:14:56.964 --> 00:14:58.098
We crashed

00:14:58.198 --> 00:15:00.700
because of your
unprovoked attack.

00:15:04.337 --> 00:15:07.007
(both growling)

00:15:16.583 --> 00:15:18.317
(device beeps)

00:15:18.318 --> 00:15:20.053
(gasps) Those ghoulish creatures

00:15:20.187 --> 00:15:22.289
trekked mud all over
our sickbay.

00:15:22.389 --> 00:15:24.391
Stay here. Guard the ship.
I'll save the crew.

00:15:24.491 --> 00:15:26.159
But, Garak,
you're just a surgeon.

00:15:26.259 --> 00:15:29.328
I am a surgeon, but not "just."

00:15:29.329 --> 00:15:30.697
(moans)

00:15:31.898 --> 00:15:33.100
(gasps)

00:15:33.233 --> 00:15:34.666
You guys seeing this?

00:15:34.667 --> 00:15:36.536
They didn't even put us
in the cell with the commanders.

00:15:36.636 --> 00:15:38.238
Eh, who cares? A cell's a cell.

00:15:38.371 --> 00:15:41.174
- Don't act like
this is our fault.
- How is it not?

00:15:41.274 --> 00:15:43.610
'Cause you've been trying
to destroy the multiverse.

00:15:43.743 --> 00:15:45.711
I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:15:45.712 --> 00:15:47.414
- Why are you so familiar?
- Oh, so then all the tears

00:15:47.514 --> 00:15:49.048
you're ripping through
the fabric of reality

00:15:49.049 --> 00:15:50.617
are just, what, for fun?

00:15:50.717 --> 00:15:53.220
We always make sure to
close them after we go through.

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:55.288
(gasp) Holy (bleep),
you're Lily Sloane.

00:15:55.422 --> 00:15:58.025
- Yeah. H-Have we met?
- MARINER: Boims.

00:15:58.125 --> 00:16:00.192
Boims. Boims, this is
"built the first warp drive

00:16:00.193 --> 00:16:01.961
with Zefram Cochrane" Lily.

00:16:02.095 --> 00:16:03.195
Wait, what?

00:16:03.196 --> 00:16:04.731
I don't know
what a warp drive is,

00:16:04.831 --> 00:16:07.234
but Zef did help me build
our quantum reality drive.

00:16:07.334 --> 00:16:10.137
Well, in this reality,
you're a depraved villain.

00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:11.537
Okay, she clearly isn't.

00:16:11.538 --> 00:16:14.707
They do not look
particularly nefarious, Captain.

00:16:14.807 --> 00:16:17.277
We are on a mission of peace,
exploring quantum realities

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:18.978
to further
our scientific knowledge.

00:16:19.112 --> 00:16:20.647
Well, then why didn't you
say something?

00:16:20.747 --> 00:16:23.550
We have directives which
dictate ethical boundaries

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:24.817
to contacting societies

00:16:24.951 --> 00:16:27.254
who can't cross realities
on their own.

00:16:27.354 --> 00:16:28.554
Well, whenever you cross
to a new reality,

00:16:28.555 --> 00:16:29.989
you leave a second rift open.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:32.792
- What?
- I told you we had not accounted

00:16:32.892 --> 00:16:34.494
for the dissipation
of additional energy.

00:16:34.594 --> 00:16:37.530
This whole time,
you weren't the bad guys.

00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:39.799
You were just a different type
of Federation.

00:16:39.899 --> 00:16:42.001
We've been stranded
from our home dimensions

00:16:42.102 --> 00:16:43.436
chasing after you.

00:16:43.536 --> 00:16:45.604
I'm sorry. I had no idea.

00:16:45.605 --> 00:16:47.474
- I believe she is
telling the truth.
- (screams)

00:16:47.574 --> 00:16:48.675
(growls)

00:16:48.775 --> 00:16:50.276
They don't like it when we talk.

00:16:50.277 --> 00:16:51.278
Then they can let us go.

00:16:51.378 --> 00:16:52.245
You hear me?

00:16:52.345 --> 00:16:54.347
Your planet su... (grunts)

00:16:54.481 --> 00:16:56.516
- (gasps)
- (growling)

00:16:57.417 --> 00:16:59.286
(gasps)

00:16:59.386 --> 00:17:03.089
- WILLIAM: Garak.
- I've never been one
for face-to-face combat.

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:05.124
(grunts) This is our doctor.

00:17:05.125 --> 00:17:07.759
Then why is he
trained in combat?

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:09.862
- (growls)
- (grunts)

00:17:09.996 --> 00:17:12.431
Old habits die hard.

00:17:12.432 --> 00:17:13.833
If you can help us
repair our ship,

00:17:13.933 --> 00:17:16.635
- I think we can get you home.
- Kim crew,

00:17:16.636 --> 00:17:18.171
- roll out.
- Let's go.

00:17:18.305 --> 00:17:20.540
Hmm.

00:17:21.674 --> 00:17:22.942
Hurry. It won't be long

00:17:23.042 --> 00:17:24.877
before some Khwopian
realizes we got out.

00:17:25.011 --> 00:17:26.946
If your team can fix
the power systems,

00:17:27.046 --> 00:17:28.515
the &lt;i&gt;Beagle&lt;/i&gt; can get to orbit.

00:17:28.615 --> 00:17:31.017
WILLIAM:
Whoa.

00:17:31.151 --> 00:17:34.053
That's an older design,
but the system should be similar

00:17:34.154 --> 00:17:35.255
to what we're used to.

00:17:35.355 --> 00:17:37.157
We should be able to manage.

00:17:39.559 --> 00:17:41.294
DAX:
Ow.

00:17:41.394 --> 00:17:42.795
Stupid patchwork (bleep).

00:17:42.895 --> 00:17:44.631
If you are fatigued,
I am able to handle this repair.

00:17:44.731 --> 00:17:47.634
Oh, you'd love to rub that in
my face, wouldn't you, Vulcan?

00:17:47.734 --> 00:17:49.168
I would not.

00:17:49.169 --> 00:17:50.503
Ugh.

00:17:51.638 --> 00:17:55.342
- So these glowsticks are
what you use to cross realities?
- Yeah.

00:17:55.442 --> 00:17:57.377
Unobserved complex gluon cores.

00:17:57.477 --> 00:17:59.746
Well, you might want to observe
a couple 'cause they're (bleep).

00:17:59.879 --> 00:18:01.781
I think we're gonna have to hit
the conduits from outside.

00:18:01.881 --> 00:18:03.983
There's an access panel
below the port stabilizers.

00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:06.352
- On it, boss.
- (William sighs)

00:18:06.353 --> 00:18:07.653
I can't believe
you actually want

00:18:07.654 --> 00:18:09.556
to explore quantum realities.

00:18:09.656 --> 00:18:10.757
You don't?

00:18:10.857 --> 00:18:12.091
I'd be happy
to never hear the word

00:18:12.225 --> 00:18:13.893
"multiverse" ever again.

00:18:14.026 --> 00:18:15.395
What's wrong with exploring?

00:18:15.528 --> 00:18:16.995
Oh, real exploring is great.

00:18:16.996 --> 00:18:19.665
We go out into the galaxy
and visit strange new worlds.

00:18:19.666 --> 00:18:22.769
What you do, isn't exploring.

00:18:23.603 --> 00:18:26.072
I must look like I'm stuck
in one spot, huh?

00:18:26.206 --> 00:18:29.409
The multiverse is just a rehash
of stuff I already know.

00:18:29.509 --> 00:18:31.444
You sound a lot like Zef.

00:18:31.544 --> 00:18:34.647
It took him a minute
to get it, too.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:39.552
&lt;i&gt;We don't need
to meet new species.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:39.652 --> 00:18:42.121
Okay, then why bother
exploring at all?

00:18:42.255 --> 00:18:44.257
To better understand ourselves.

00:18:44.357 --> 00:18:46.426
It's fun to learn about aliens,

00:18:46.526 --> 00:18:48.127
but learning about humanity,

00:18:48.261 --> 00:18:49.896
that's something else.

00:18:49.996 --> 00:18:53.666
I've met humans who've built
rings around the sun.

00:18:53.766 --> 00:18:56.403
I've met others whose ships
are the size of continents.

00:18:56.503 --> 00:18:59.071
I'm learning
about what humans can be.

00:18:59.172 --> 00:19:01.240
Mapping our potential.

00:19:01.241 --> 00:19:03.776
So far, it's limitless.

00:19:03.876 --> 00:19:06.579
I never thought about it
like that.

00:19:06.679 --> 00:19:07.880
Look at Mariner.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:10.517
Your friendship
transcends realities.

00:19:10.617 --> 00:19:13.820
Trust like that is
powerful stuff.

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.053
- (ship rumbling)
- (all clamoring)

00:19:15.054 --> 00:19:16.789
(Mariner shouting)

00:19:16.923 --> 00:19:19.326
(grunts)
Is that supposed to happen?

00:19:19.426 --> 00:19:21.828
SLOANE:
Someone's stealing my ship!

00:19:25.498 --> 00:19:26.899
We need to get back to the &lt;i&gt;Nax!&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:32.572
(growling)

00:19:32.672 --> 00:19:33.973
(grunts)

00:19:34.073 --> 00:19:35.274
We don't have time for this!

00:19:35.275 --> 00:19:36.575
I do.

00:19:36.576 --> 00:19:38.878
(shouts, laughing)

00:19:41.748 --> 00:19:42.649
(shouts)

00:19:42.749 --> 00:19:44.284
Yah! (laughs)

00:19:45.818 --> 00:19:47.787
(grunting)

00:19:47.887 --> 00:19:49.689
Keep going.

00:19:49.822 --> 00:19:51.790
This is how I relax. Calm down.

00:19:51.791 --> 00:19:54.361
Everybody's going
to get their asses kicked.

00:19:54.494 --> 00:19:56.028
Curzon, be careful!

00:19:56.128 --> 00:19:58.398
(exhales)
My freaking calves.

00:19:58.498 --> 00:20:00.433
Stupid bog planet.
So much wading.

00:20:00.533 --> 00:20:02.669
Open hailing frequencies,
all channels.

00:20:03.836 --> 00:20:05.103
This is Captain William Boimler.

00:20:05.104 --> 00:20:06.539
Whoever's piloting that ship,

00:20:06.673 --> 00:20:08.375
you need to return
to the surface now.

00:20:08.475 --> 00:20:11.177
&lt;i&gt;Why? So you can take
all these beautiful Kims&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:11.278 --> 00:20:12.912
&lt;i&gt;back to their home universes
where they'll be&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:13.012 --> 00:20:14.514
&lt;i&gt;overlooked and disrespected?&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:14.614 --> 00:20:16.449
Kim, what the hell
are you doing?

00:20:16.549 --> 00:20:17.550
&lt;i&gt;He tricked us, Captain.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:18.984
&lt;i&gt;We don't want to be here.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:18.985 --> 00:20:20.652
&lt;i&gt;I'm taking you
back to my universe&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:20.653 --> 00:20:22.355
&lt;i&gt;where Harry Kims can rank up.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:22.489 --> 00:20:24.023
Hey, we didn't finish
the repairs.

00:20:24.123 --> 00:20:25.558
The &lt;i&gt;Beagle&lt;/i&gt; can't maintain
a fifth dimension

00:20:25.658 --> 00:20:27.126
without subspace gluons!

00:20:27.226 --> 00:20:29.396
&lt;i&gt;Spewing engineering nonsense
won't work on me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:29.529 --> 00:20:31.063
&lt;i&gt;I've got two pips!&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:32.064 --> 00:20:34.666
Curzon, get us into orbit.

00:20:34.667 --> 00:20:35.735
Aye, Captain.

00:20:35.868 --> 00:20:37.136
You are limping.

00:20:37.236 --> 00:20:39.706
I should've stretched
before that workout.

00:20:44.777 --> 00:20:48.146
We have to stop him
from crossing into another QR!

00:20:48.147 --> 00:20:49.815
Without repairs,
he's flying a bomb

00:20:49.816 --> 00:20:51.884
that could spread
to all universes!

00:20:51.984 --> 00:20:54.086
The death toll
would be beyond measure.

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:55.888
Damn you, two-pip Kim!

00:20:56.022 --> 00:20:57.724
Why hasn't he opened a rift?

00:20:57.857 --> 00:20:59.991
The &lt;i&gt;Beagle&lt;/i&gt; won't allow it until
he's out of the gravity well.

00:20:59.992 --> 00:21:02.061
We will not make it in time
at this speed.

00:21:02.161 --> 00:21:03.829
Permission to try
and juice the engines?

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:05.298
Granted.

00:21:10.337 --> 00:21:12.104
(grunts)
Why won't you work?

00:21:12.204 --> 00:21:14.941
Hey, this un-Kim-like behavior, pal.

00:21:15.041 --> 00:21:16.876
- Shut up, Harry!
- You shut up, Harry!

00:21:16.976 --> 00:21:18.878
&lt;i&gt;COMPUTER:
Gravity well cleared.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:18.978 --> 00:21:20.613
Ha-ha! I got it.

00:21:22.214 --> 00:21:24.083
&lt;i&gt;Impulse increased by 15%.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:24.183 --> 00:21:26.319
&lt;i&gt;(all shouting)&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:26.419 --> 00:21:28.019
The &lt;i&gt;Beagle's&lt;/i&gt; falling apart.

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:31.324
Brace yourselves
for a better life, Kims.

00:21:35.728 --> 00:21:37.930
Damn it! He's making a rift.

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:39.766
Despite our increase in speed,
we will not be

00:21:39.899 --> 00:21:41.133
close enough to intervene.

00:21:41.267 --> 00:21:42.769
Well, then we need
to do a micro warp jump.

00:21:42.869 --> 00:21:44.202
The tachyon levels are too high.

00:21:44.203 --> 00:21:45.605
Our engines would overload.

00:21:45.705 --> 00:21:47.774
How are we supposed to stop them
and not blow up?

00:21:47.874 --> 00:21:51.143
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Beagle's &lt;i&gt;creating waves
of gravitational turbulence.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:51.277 --> 00:21:52.979
And that's a good thing?

00:21:53.112 --> 00:21:54.614
It means mass matters.

00:21:54.714 --> 00:21:56.616
If I can increase the gravity
around the warp port,

00:21:56.749 --> 00:21:57.984
it'll be a tachyon shield,

00:21:58.084 --> 00:21:59.285
and we can go
as fast as you want.

00:21:59.419 --> 00:22:00.787
But won't that crush you?

00:22:00.887 --> 00:22:02.455
Let's pretend
I'm the adventurous Mariner

00:22:02.555 --> 00:22:04.357
from your reality
who's okay risking it.

00:22:04.457 --> 00:22:06.459
- Mariner--
- (alert sounding)

00:22:06.559 --> 00:22:08.427
(grunts) (bleep)

00:22:08.428 --> 00:22:09.362
(shouts)

00:22:09.462 --> 00:22:12.632
(moaning)

00:22:14.801 --> 00:22:17.370
Thought you could use
a holographic hand.

00:22:19.071 --> 00:22:22.174
Engineering is
at ten times gravity, Captain.

00:22:22.274 --> 00:22:23.476
Curzon, warp us now!

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:25.712
- (Dax grunting)
- Dax?

00:22:25.812 --> 00:22:28.580
Stupid salamander zapped me.

00:22:28.581 --> 00:22:30.517
Get him to sickbay!

00:22:31.317 --> 00:22:33.686
- Mariner, I hope you're right.
- (beeps)

00:22:36.923 --> 00:22:39.058
♪ ♪

00:22:41.127 --> 00:22:43.329
Ah, it worked, the warp core's
not overloading.

00:22:43.430 --> 00:22:44.363
Great.

00:22:44.464 --> 00:22:45.698
Shut off...

00:22:45.832 --> 00:22:47.333
the gravity.

00:22:47.434 --> 00:22:48.768
Oh, right, sorry.

00:22:48.868 --> 00:22:49.768
(whirring slows)

00:22:49.769 --> 00:22:51.904
(exhales, panting)

00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:56.008
There's nothing more I can do.

00:22:56.142 --> 00:22:59.211
- If we had had more time.
- Thank you, Doctor.

00:23:02.415 --> 00:23:05.817
Garak, you do know
I'll follow you to any reality.

00:23:05.818 --> 00:23:07.854
I'd do the same for you.
I really don't care

00:23:07.954 --> 00:23:10.222
where we end up
as long as we're together.

00:23:10.356 --> 00:23:12.525
What?
Then why have we been arguing?

00:23:12.625 --> 00:23:13.659
Because it's fun.

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:15.928
No, it's not!

00:23:18.364 --> 00:23:19.298
(laughs)

00:23:19.398 --> 00:23:21.133
Nobody stops Harry Kim.

00:23:21.233 --> 00:23:22.435
(grunts)

00:23:22.535 --> 00:23:23.702
What are you doing?

00:23:23.703 --> 00:23:25.137
We have to transport
out of here.

00:23:25.237 --> 00:23:28.107
Why? I'm offering you
a better life.

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:29.442
If that's what it takes,

00:23:29.576 --> 00:23:30.842
- we don't want it.
- What are you-- Hey!

00:23:30.843 --> 00:23:33.646
- No!
- Grab him!

00:23:33.746 --> 00:23:35.114
(coughs)

00:23:35.247 --> 00:23:38.250
Well, at least you get
a front row seat

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:39.952
to my demise.

00:23:40.086 --> 00:23:42.589
I take no pleasure
in seeing my friend perish.

00:23:42.689 --> 00:23:45.157
Since when are we friends?

00:23:45.257 --> 00:23:47.627
- Since the day we met.
- (coughing)

00:23:47.727 --> 00:23:49.295
I know.

00:23:49.395 --> 00:23:51.163
Dax had a good run.

00:23:51.263 --> 00:23:53.700
Too bad that it has to end
with me.

00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:57.336
I will remove your symbiont
and return it to your reality.

00:23:57.436 --> 00:23:59.606
(gasps)
Won't work without a host.

00:23:59.706 --> 00:24:02.408
Then I must attempt to transfer
your shared memories

00:24:02.509 --> 00:24:04.276
from Dax itself.

00:24:09.616 --> 00:24:11.117
(Kims grunting, clamoring)

00:24:11.217 --> 00:24:12.751
Fine!

00:24:12.752 --> 00:24:15.386
You Kims are too weak to know
a good thing when you have it.

00:24:15.387 --> 00:24:17.222
You want to know
why you're all still ensigns?

00:24:17.223 --> 00:24:18.625
This, this is why.

00:24:18.758 --> 00:24:20.860
You don't deserve
to come with me.

00:24:24.396 --> 00:24:25.732
- KIMS: Whoa.
- Welcome back, Kims.

00:24:25.832 --> 00:24:27.133
Good to be back, sir.

00:24:27.266 --> 00:24:28.768
Can you get
a tractor beam on him?

00:24:28.868 --> 00:24:30.369
Negative, he's too far.

00:24:30.469 --> 00:24:31.838
- Then target engines.
- No!

00:24:31.971 --> 00:24:34.340
If you open fire now,
it'll just make it worse!

00:24:34.440 --> 00:24:36.809
Worse than destroying
all realities?!

00:24:38.611 --> 00:24:39.846
Harry, you have to stop.

00:24:39.946 --> 00:24:41.112
That ship won't make it.

00:24:41.113 --> 00:24:42.414
&lt;i&gt;Nice try.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:42.515 --> 00:24:44.517
I'm Harry (bleep) Kim.

00:24:44.651 --> 00:24:46.819
And you don't get
to order me around.

00:24:46.919 --> 00:24:49.088
(laughing)

00:24:50.623 --> 00:24:52.191
(cackles)

00:25:00.800 --> 00:25:02.569
- (shouting)
- (grunting)

00:25:13.179 --> 00:25:14.346
That was...

00:25:14.480 --> 00:25:17.383
more katra
than I had anticipated.

00:25:17.483 --> 00:25:18.951
(coughing)

00:25:19.051 --> 00:25:20.687
You back Dax up

00:25:20.820 --> 00:25:23.454
in that big Vulcan brain.

00:25:23.455 --> 00:25:27.226
I will protect and pass them on.

00:25:27.326 --> 00:25:30.296
Maybe you're not so bad.

00:25:30.396 --> 00:25:32.899
For a Vulcan.

00:25:32.999 --> 00:25:36.202
(monitor flatlines)

00:25:39.538 --> 00:25:40.773
(all gasp)

00:25:45.377 --> 00:25:47.179
Lily, what's happening?

00:25:47.279 --> 00:25:50.049
The explosion disrupted
the coherence of the rift.

00:25:50.149 --> 00:25:52.984
Soliton waves will spread
across all quantum realities.

00:25:52.985 --> 00:25:55.186
No, no, there has
to be something we can do.

00:25:55.187 --> 00:25:57.089
This ship has
a force beam generator?

00:25:57.189 --> 00:25:58.257
A deflector? Yeah.

00:25:58.390 --> 00:25:59.959
With a directed soliton burst,

00:26:00.059 --> 00:26:02.995
I could use it to guide the wave
into a single reality.

00:26:03.095 --> 00:26:07.032
But then won't you be dooming an
entire universe to be destroyed?

00:26:07.033 --> 00:26:09.168
It's either one or all.

00:26:09.268 --> 00:26:11.703
We need a reality
that can respond to the threat.

00:26:11.704 --> 00:26:13.239
I know where to send it.

00:26:13.339 --> 00:26:14.907
Scan me. Use my reality.

00:26:15.041 --> 00:26:17.009
What? Boims, no.

00:26:17.109 --> 00:26:18.778
- Are you sure?
- WILLIAM: No.

00:26:18.911 --> 00:26:21.413
But I'm there and so are you.

00:26:21.513 --> 00:26:23.182
And Tendi and Rutherford.

00:26:23.282 --> 00:26:25.584
I know they can figure out
a solution.

00:26:25.685 --> 00:26:28.454
Why would you do this
to your friends?

00:26:28.587 --> 00:26:30.757
Because he trusts them.

00:26:30.890 --> 00:26:33.926
And that trust transcends
quantum realities.

00:26:34.727 --> 00:26:36.629
Activate the soliton beam.

00:26:38.064 --> 00:26:39.666
(computer trilling)

00:26:47.473 --> 00:26:49.809
Done. I hope you're right.

00:26:49.942 --> 00:26:52.111
I piggybacked a message
to my duplicate.

00:26:52.244 --> 00:26:53.780
- He'll know what to do.
- Will he?

00:26:53.880 --> 00:26:56.415
Yeah, as long
as he doesn't freak out.

00:26:59.218 --> 00:27:00.920
Holy (bleep)!

00:27:01.020 --> 00:27:03.554
We're all gonna die!

00:27:03.555 --> 00:27:07.026
&lt;i&gt;- (Boimler screaming)
- (objects crashing)&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:12.631 --> 00:27:14.834
♪

00:27:43.896 --> 00:27:45.564
♪ ♪

00:28:02.014 --> 00:28:03.716
(man imitates weapons firing)

00:28:05.551 --> 00:28:07.185
Chirp.

00:28:07.186 --> 00:28:09.722
